{"type":"text","timestamp":1788503861066,"sessionID":"ses_f94e4d0f6ffeQOYRYclieGJzVe","part":{"id":"prt_06b230d99001AbNglOUDF6slyo","messageID":"msg_06b22fc13001UEIKa3NZM0PKt7","sessionID":"ses_f94e4d0f6ffeQOYRYclieGJzVe","type":"text","text":"All changes are complete in `src/agents/realtime/session.py`:\n\n1. **Removed background task management** — deleted the `_background_task` attribute (`session.py:83`) and the `asyncio.create_task` call. `function_call` events are now awaited directly in `on_event` via `await self._handle_tool_call(event)` (`session.py:148-149`), so tool calls (tool_start → invoke → send_tool_output → tool_end) process fully within the main event flow.\n\n2. **`_get_new_history` is now a `@classmethod`** (`session.py:243`) — callable as `RealtimeSession._get_new_history(...)`, handling both merging transcription transcripts into placeholder `input_audio` user messages and inserting/replacing items by `item_id` / `previous_item_id`.\n\n3. **Simplified `close()`** (`session.py:125-129`) — now just sets `_closed`, removes the listener, and closes the model; no task cancellation logic.\n\n4. **Added `tests/realtime/test_session.py`** with 8 tests covering inline tool call handling (no `_background_task` attribute, ordered tool_start/tool_end events), classmethod-based history updates (transcript merging, replace-existing, insert-after-previous, append fallback), and listener/model cleanup on close.\n\nAll 17 realtime tests pass; `ruff format`, `ruff check`, and `mypy` are clean. The 16 failures elsewhere in the suite are pre-existing environment issues (verified against the original code).","time":{"start":1788503854489,"end":1788503861061}}}
